{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f28ad3dd-5f76-4364-ab76-0ebc202e76c3",
    "name": "Tesla Fleet Energy Backup Time Of Use API",
    "description": "The energy_sites surface of the Tesla Fleet API. Lets OAuth-authorized partners and owners read\nPowerwall, Solar, and Megapack site state \u2014 site info, live status, calendar history, programs \u2014\nand write backup reserve, operation mode (self_consumption, backup, autonomous), storm mode,\ntime-of-use settings, and off-grid vehicle charging reserve.\n\nAuthentication uses Tesla Fleet API OAuth 2.0 with the energy_device_data (read) and\nenergy_cmds (write) scopes. Third-party applications must register a partner account on the\nTesla Developer Portal and pair a virtual key with the owner's account.\n\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Tesla Developer Support",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "createdAt": "2026-07-28T03:10:34.000Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-07-28T03:10:34.000Z",
    "lastUpdatedBy": "35240",
    "uid": "35240-f28ad3dd-5f76-4364-ab76-0ebc202e76c3"
  },
